      "content": "Thanks for the draft. It sounds professional, but I'm looking at the preview of the CDS (Customer Delight Score) in the system, and it's sitting at a 0.62. For an enterprise client losing this much money, we really need to make sure they feel heard and supported, so we want that score closer to 0.9 or 1.0 to avoid a churn escalation.\n\nCan you revise this to be much more empathetic and positive? Just remember what I said earlier—don't lose the technical focus, but try to lean into a more reassuring and upbeat tone so they don't feel so stressed.",
